# CASES below copies each case's RUN lines from its .test or .mlir file until
# that case's switch commit deletes them there; until then, edit both copies.
"""The CTNative/Lowering lit cases that have no test of their own in a driver,
as pytest tests: those whose Python step runs among other RUN lines, and
those with no Python step (FileCheck, -verify-diagnostics and compiled
programs). test_case is parametrized over CASES, whose keys are the
cases' lit paths relative to this folder without .test or .mlir:
`test_case[Closures/direct-callbacks]` is lit's `ctcompile ::
CTNative/Lowering/Closures/direct-callbacks.mlir`. Each test runs all of its
case's RUN lines in order through lit_lines.run, every line under bash, as lit
runs them.
"""

